{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmARmq2HSVZv7QdwttHv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten the candidate (`streak_weary_chance_pseudoflip`) and it passes the self-check, which prints `OK`. That check only fits one short chain, so it can't confirm the model will pass admission's convergence test on the full fit.\n\n**Hypothesis (unchanged from the rejected attempt):** this refines the incumbent `short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution`. The one change is to people's idea of a fair coin: they think it gets more likely to switch the longer the current streak has lasted (a gambler's-fallacy term, with one fitted rise per extra flip, taken from `gamblers_run_second_order_side_habit`). So the first one or two breaks in a long streak make a sequence look much more random. This targets the critique finding that survives the FDR correction: in long pairs where both sequences switch at most twice, people pick the more-switching sequence more often than the incumbent predicts.\n\n**Why the first attempt failed:** I opened its cached fit. Three of the four chains agreed. The fourth got stuck in a separate, degenerate solution where the imagined trick coin is almost certainly rigged towards tails (`s_heads` ≈ 0.02, against ≈ 0.49 in the other chains). That chain dragged the other main parameters with it, giving R-hat 1.53. The new streak term itself (`g_run` ≈ 0.09) came out the same in all four chains, so it was not the cause.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Trick-coin prior:** I tightened the prior on the trick coin's heads-lean parameter from Normal(0, 1) to Normal(0, 0.5). The data put this parameter near 0, and the stuck chain's value of about −3.9 is now far outside the prior. This is a prior change for convergence, not a change to the mechanism, and it's noted in the docstring.\n- **Streak-term prior:** I tightened the prior on `g_run` from Normal(0, 1) to Normal(0, 0.3), because its input feature can reach about ±15 for long streaks.\n\n**Self-check:** the 1-chain, 100-draw smoke fit gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −3565.4, against −3566.8 for the incumbent's full fit. That comparison is only rough on so few draws. It also flagged 6.2% of trials with high Pareto-k, which makes that ELPD figure unreliable. I'd expect that to drop with a full-length fit, but haven't checked. The check doesn't test novelty either. A second rejection ends this slot."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":106294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":403,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e4577b7-5159-43ab-8c6c-88f7df60dddf","uuid":"879f2c5e-0c35-476a-8d07-9400239ccc92","timestamp":"2026-10-06T14:45:20.951Z","request_id":"req_011CfmARmNVERwhAFjM8cSgD"}
